WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.935
-Well, after six months
of quarantine,

00:00:02.935 --> 00:00:06.406
during which I rapidly descended
into isolation-induced madness,

00:00:06.406 --> 00:00:09.275
we're back in our studio here
at 30 Rock in New York City.

00:00:09.275 --> 00:00:13.913
And, well, you guys, it's just
nice to be around people again.

00:00:13.913 --> 00:00:16.181
And, as promised, now that
we're back in the studio,

00:00:16.181 --> 00:00:18.550
I will no longer have
my old friend the Sea Captain

00:00:18.550 --> 00:00:21.487
by my side to interject
with his annoying wordplay.

00:00:21.487 --> 00:00:23.757
Although I do feel an obligation
to check in on him

00:00:23.757 --> 00:00:25.525
once in a while
as he works his way

00:00:25.525 --> 00:00:29.195
through the 1977 classic novel
"The Thorn Birds."

00:00:29.195 --> 00:00:32.632
-[ Laughs ] Oh, oh, you go,
Meggie Cleary.

00:00:32.632 --> 00:00:34.167
-Hey, relax.
I don't miss him either.

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:36.468
The dude smelled like clams
and he had like 50 jokes

00:00:36.468 --> 00:00:38.371
with the punch line "Land, ho."

00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:40.072
Anyway, now that
we're back in the studio,

00:00:40.072 --> 00:00:41.407
I give you my solemn oath

00:00:41.407 --> 00:00:43.776
there will be no more talking
inanimate objects

00:00:43.776 --> 00:00:45.845
that interrupt the flow
of "A Closer Look"

00:00:45.845 --> 00:00:47.346
with their ridiculous
interjections.

00:00:47.346 --> 00:00:49.749
And speaking of
ridiculous interjections...

00:00:49.749 --> 00:00:52.485
-New York's hottest
club is Segue.

00:00:55.021 --> 00:00:56.555
-The president held another fake

00:00:56.555 --> 00:00:58.858
press conference-slash-campaign
rally at the White House

00:00:58.858 --> 00:01:00.526
where he pretended
everything's great

00:01:00.526 --> 00:01:02.795
as the coronavirus pandemic
continues to rage,

00:01:02.795 --> 00:01:05.598
and now he's trying to pretend
he's anti-war in response

00:01:05.598 --> 00:01:07.266
to the news
that he insulted veterans.

00:01:07.266 --> 00:01:10.002
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:01:10.002 --> 00:01:13.940
♪♪

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:15.542
Now that Labor Day is behind us,

00:01:15.542 --> 00:01:17.243
we're entering
the traditional home stretch

00:01:17.243 --> 00:01:18.611
of the presidential campaign.

00:01:18.611 --> 00:01:20.413
And for some perspective,
I think it's worth

00:01:20.413 --> 00:01:21.647
stepping back two weeks

00:01:21.647 --> 00:01:23.249
to the Republican
National Convention

00:01:23.249 --> 00:01:26.051
when we were all anxiously
sitting in front of our TVs

00:01:26.051 --> 00:01:28.521
saying,
"Do people actually like this?"

00:01:28.521 --> 00:01:30.456
Kind of like how you feel
when you're watching

00:01:30.456 --> 00:01:31.891
one of those TikTok videos

00:01:31.891 --> 00:01:34.159
where someone eats cereal
out of someone else's mouth

00:01:34.159 --> 00:01:36.095
and you have to wonder,
"Is this a thing now?

00:01:36.095 --> 00:01:37.496
Will my kids do this one day?

00:01:37.496 --> 00:01:40.199
And when I tell them
not to do it, will they scream

00:01:40.199 --> 00:01:42.602
that I don't understand anything
and then run to their rooms

00:01:42.602 --> 00:01:46.005
and slam the door over this --
over this [bleep] nonsense?"

00:01:46.005 --> 00:01:47.707
Anyway, you remember the RNC

00:01:47.707 --> 00:01:50.042
when the president
flagrantly broke the law

00:01:50.042 --> 00:01:52.378
by holding a political event
on the White House lawn

00:01:52.378 --> 00:01:54.881
when the Republican Party
decided to celebrate

00:01:54.881 --> 00:01:56.950
threats of violence
against protesters

00:01:56.950 --> 00:01:59.652
by giving Mr. and Mrs.
Elmer Dudd over here

00:01:59.652 --> 00:02:00.986
a prominent speaking spot?

00:02:00.986 --> 00:02:03.857
Or how about when
a profusely sweating

00:02:03.857 --> 00:02:07.760
Rudy Giuliani mopped his brow,
then rubbed his weirdo juice

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:10.096
all over that lady
sitting next to him?

00:02:10.096 --> 00:02:12.598
That's like when you touch
a baby bird.

00:02:12.598 --> 00:02:14.967
Now her mother's going to have
to stop feeding her.

00:02:14.967 --> 00:02:17.503
That's the way you sweat
when you wake up from a dream

00:02:17.503 --> 00:02:20.139
where you were sitting next to
Rudy Giuliani.

00:02:20.139 --> 00:02:22.875
"Oh! Oh, thank God.
Aah!"

00:02:22.875 --> 00:02:24.210
How about when
Republicans thought

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:26.846
this would be a convincing
campaign message?

00:02:26.846 --> 00:02:29.815
-Joe Biden is basically the
Loch Ness monster of the swamp.

00:02:29.815 --> 00:02:32.251
-They'll disarm you,
empty the prisons,

00:02:32.251 --> 00:02:33.652
lock you in your home,

00:02:33.652 --> 00:02:36.255
and invite MS-13
to live next door.

00:02:36.255 --> 00:02:38.290
-We may not have realized
it at the time,

00:02:38.290 --> 00:02:42.996
but Trump is the bodyguard
of Western civilization.

00:02:42.996 --> 00:02:46.132
-Ladies and gentlemen,
leaders and fighters

00:02:46.132 --> 00:02:47.700
for freedom and liberty

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:53.772
and the American dream,
the best is yet to come!

00:02:53.772 --> 00:02:56.108
-Jesus, are you campaigning
or trying to scare

00:02:56.108 --> 00:02:58.745
some seagulls away
from your beach blanket?

00:02:58.745 --> 00:03:02.015
"Those Doritos are not for you!"

00:03:02.015 --> 00:03:05.751
I hope the GOP platform added
"Replace everyone's TV screens."

00:03:05.751 --> 00:03:07.453
Well, you're not going
to believe this.

00:03:07.453 --> 00:03:09.755
But according to polls,
none of it worked.

00:03:09.755 --> 00:03:12.625
A new CNN poll had Joe Biden
ahead of Trump by eight points,

00:03:12.625 --> 00:03:14.660
which matches the national
polling average.

00:03:14.660 --> 00:03:17.797
It is basically where the race
has been since June.

00:03:17.797 --> 00:03:19.932
Trump could've disappeared
for three months

00:03:19.932 --> 00:03:21.100
and it would've had
the same effect.

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:23.002
In fact, that's basically
what he did.

00:03:23.002 --> 00:03:25.471
Dude plays golf with more
B-list celebrities

00:03:25.471 --> 00:03:26.972
than the Pebble Beach Pro Am.

00:03:26.972 --> 00:03:29.709
"This weekend on CBS, watch
Huey Lewis and the guy

00:03:29.709 --> 00:03:31.644
who voiced the Budweiser frogs

00:03:31.644 --> 00:03:33.879
miss a two-foot putt
for triple bogey."

00:03:33.879 --> 00:03:36.549
And a CBS poll out on Sunday
asked voters

00:03:36.549 --> 00:03:38.985
specifically who would do
a better job with protests

00:03:38.985 --> 00:03:42.622
and criminal justice issues,
and the answers did not support

00:03:42.622 --> 00:03:44.757
Trump's so-called
law and order strategy.

00:03:44.757 --> 00:03:46.325
-We've seen the president
try to shift

00:03:46.325 --> 00:03:49.061
what this conversation
is about in this election.

00:03:49.061 --> 00:03:51.097
He wants it to be not about
COVID-19

00:03:51.097 --> 00:03:53.265
but about violence
in the cities.

00:03:53.265 --> 00:03:55.702
What do your numbers
tell you about that strategy?

00:03:55.702 --> 00:03:58.404
-Biden comes out better
on that measure,

00:03:58.404 --> 00:04:01.607
and particularly we asked
if each candidate seemed

00:04:01.607 --> 00:04:03.276
to be trying
to calm the situation

00:04:03.276 --> 00:04:06.379
or maybe encourage
even more tension.

00:04:06.379 --> 00:04:08.948
Well, the president
on balance is seen

00:04:08.948 --> 00:04:11.950
as encouraging more tension,
more fighting.

00:04:11.950 --> 00:04:13.219
-And of course he is.

00:04:13.219 --> 00:04:14.821
He's not exactly
a calming presence.

00:04:14.821 --> 00:04:17.022
He dresses like retired
Darth Vader.

00:04:17.022 --> 00:04:20.059
He yells like he's on the other
side of six lanes of traffic.

00:04:20.059 --> 00:04:23.229
And even his smile looks like it
was directed by Stanley Kubrick.

00:04:23.229 --> 00:04:26.032
He's the human embodiment
of tension and fighting.

00:04:26.032 --> 00:04:28.234
He's the uncle at the wedding
reception

00:04:28.234 --> 00:04:30.470
who has the rest of the family
on pins and needles

00:04:30.470 --> 00:04:33.272
because they're afraid he'll get
drunk and give a speech.

00:04:33.272 --> 00:04:34.973
"I -- I didn't want --
I never thought --

00:04:34.973 --> 00:04:37.243
I never thought it would
work out after Tyler

00:04:37.243 --> 00:04:38.577
cheated on Tammy.

00:04:38.577 --> 00:04:40.279
Also, don't believe
what you hear.

00:04:40.279 --> 00:04:43.549
I did not have a series
of mini strokes."

00:04:43.549 --> 00:04:44.883
I mean, who wouldn't prefer
the uncle

00:04:44.883 --> 00:04:46.352
who doesn't come to the wedding

00:04:46.352 --> 00:04:48.988
because Amtrak doesn't service
Catalina Island?

00:04:48.988 --> 00:04:51.691
Second, Trump and his allies
have been open about this.

00:04:51.691 --> 00:04:53.926
They don't want to
calm things down.

00:04:53.926 --> 00:04:57.229
They actually want things
to get worse, not better.

00:04:57.229 --> 00:04:59.698
Because they think
they can blame it on Joe Biden.

00:04:59.698 --> 00:05:01.601
Kellyanne Conway came out
and said it outright.

00:05:01.601 --> 00:05:03.536
That's why Trump and his
attorney general

00:05:03.536 --> 00:05:06.639
moved to classified
Democratic cities as, quote,

00:05:06.639 --> 00:05:09.708
"anarchist jurisdictions"
in an insane

00:05:09.708 --> 00:05:11.911
and deeply
authoritarian memo last week.

00:05:11.911 --> 00:05:14.680
And it's why Trump tweeted
this last night.

00:05:14.680 --> 00:05:16.782
"The real polls are starting
to look great.

00:05:16.782 --> 00:05:20.686
We will be having an even bigger
victory than that of 2016.

00:05:20.686 --> 00:05:23.723
The radical left anarchists,
agitators, looters,

00:05:23.723 --> 00:05:25.891
and just plain lunatics
will not be happy,

00:05:25.891 --> 00:05:27.392
but they will behave."

00:05:27.392 --> 00:05:28.727
They'll behave?

00:05:28.727 --> 00:05:30.563
It's never reassuring when
the president talks

00:05:30.563 --> 00:05:32.431
about his political opponents
like a dean

00:05:32.431 --> 00:05:35.902
trying to shut down a rowdy frat
in an '80s teen comedy.

00:05:35.902 --> 00:05:37.303
"I'm outlawing toga parties.

00:05:37.303 --> 00:05:39.671
The gentlemen from Theta
Delta Psi will not be happy,

00:05:39.671 --> 00:05:41.039
but they will behave.

00:05:41.039 --> 00:05:43.442
And as this is the end of act
two of this team romp,

00:05:43.442 --> 00:05:46.412
I am confident that this will be
the final outcome of things.

00:05:46.412 --> 00:05:48.381
Hello?
Oh, it's the boys from Theta.

00:05:48.381 --> 00:05:49.848
Oh, you do?

00:05:49.848 --> 00:05:51.250
Oh, they're asking me to ride
on their homecoming float.

00:05:51.250 --> 00:05:53.386
I told you they respond
to a little bit of discipline.

00:05:53.386 --> 00:05:55.555
And just to be clear, boys,
you want me to wear pants that

00:05:55.555 --> 00:05:57.723
are loose enough to fall down
if my belt somehow came off?

00:05:57.723 --> 00:06:00.959
Well, consider it done
and I look forward to it."

00:06:00.959 --> 00:06:02.194
Look, guys,
we're back in the studio,

00:06:02.194 --> 00:06:03.629
but we're still
going to take tangents.

00:06:03.629 --> 00:06:04.897
Where were we?
Oh, right.

00:06:04.897 --> 00:06:06.698
The real world.
Trump's strategy isn't working.

00:06:06.698 --> 00:06:07.933
Poll after poll has shown

00:06:07.933 --> 00:06:09.568
that the American people
can see through it.

00:06:09.568 --> 00:06:11.704
For one thing, Trump can't
call himself

00:06:11.704 --> 00:06:12.939
the law
and order candidate

00:06:12.939 --> 00:06:15.274
when he surrounds himself
with criminal goons.

00:06:15.274 --> 00:06:17.242
Just take, for example,
Louis DeJoy,

00:06:17.242 --> 00:06:19.245
who is Trump's
postmaster general.

00:06:19.245 --> 00:06:20.880
Despite having a name
that makes him sound

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:23.549
like a puppet
on a French children's show --

00:06:23.549 --> 00:06:30.089
[ Speaking French ]

00:06:30.089 --> 00:06:31.323
Louis DeJoy...

00:06:31.323 --> 00:06:35.561
[ Continues in French ]

00:06:35.561 --> 00:06:37.696
This weekend --
[ Laughs ]

00:06:37.696 --> 00:06:40.666
My mother was my French teacher.
That's the best I could do.

00:06:40.666 --> 00:06:42.602
This weekend it was reported
that DeJoy,

00:06:42.602 --> 00:06:44.770
a major GOP donor
with tens of millions of dollars

00:06:44.770 --> 00:06:47.206
and conflicts of interest
may have illegally pressured

00:06:47.206 --> 00:06:48.907
employees
to donate to Republicans,

00:06:48.907 --> 00:06:50.642
then reimbursed them
with bonuses,

00:06:50.642 --> 00:06:53.245
which must've really sucked
for his employees.

00:06:53.245 --> 00:06:56.448
"Okay, honey, the good news is
I got a bonus of $50,000.

00:06:56.448 --> 00:06:58.317
The bad news is I have to
give it to Mitch McConnell.

00:06:58.317 --> 00:07:00.152
Don't be mad, honey.
Where are you going, honey?"

00:07:00.152 --> 00:07:01.587
At his press conference
yesterday,

00:07:01.587 --> 00:07:04.623
Trump was asked if he would
be okay with removing

00:07:04.623 --> 00:07:05.992
DeJoy from his post.

00:07:05.992 --> 00:07:08.461
And he quickly pivoted
to complaining

00:07:08.461 --> 00:07:10.863
about the many
investigations of him.

00:07:10.863 --> 00:07:13.065
-Would you support
an investigation, sir?

00:07:13.065 --> 00:07:14.500
-Sure, sure.
-And in --

00:07:14.500 --> 00:07:17.036
-I think let
the investigations go.

00:07:17.036 --> 00:07:20.272
But -- but he's
a very respected man.

00:07:20.272 --> 00:07:22.809
-If it's proven to be
a campaign finance scheme,

00:07:22.809 --> 00:07:24.710
do you think
he should lose his job?

00:07:24.710 --> 00:07:26.112
-Yeah, if something
could be proven

00:07:26.112 --> 00:07:27.847
that he did something wrong,
always.

00:07:27.847 --> 00:07:29.048
-Thank you.
-Always.

00:07:29.048 --> 00:07:32.351
They've been looking at me
for four years.

00:07:32.351 --> 00:07:33.852
They found nothing.

00:07:33.852 --> 00:07:35.221
Four years.
Think of it.

00:07:35.221 --> 00:07:37.523
For four years, from the day
I came down the escalator,

00:07:37.523 --> 00:07:41.827
I've been under investigation by
sleeze, and they found nothing.

00:07:41.827 --> 00:07:43.496
-No, they did not find nothing.

00:07:43.496 --> 00:07:45.030
If anything,
they found too much.

00:07:45.030 --> 00:07:47.433
Somewhere in the FBI
there's a file cabinet labeled

00:07:47.433 --> 00:07:49.034
"Trump's crimes
we didn't have time for."

00:07:49.034 --> 00:07:50.703
I'm pretty sure I saw the room

00:07:50.703 --> 00:07:52.138
where they keep
the evidence against Trump

00:07:52.138 --> 00:07:53.539
on an episode of "Hoarders."

00:07:53.539 --> 00:07:55.140
They found among other things,

00:07:55.140 --> 00:07:56.509
two separate criminal
conspiracies

00:07:56.509 --> 00:07:58.311
to help get you elected,
at least ten instances

00:07:58.311 --> 00:08:00.145
of possible obstruction
of justice,

00:08:00.145 --> 00:08:02.548
and a whole other separate thing
you got impeached for.

00:08:02.548 --> 00:08:04.617
Just because you're
not in jail yet

00:08:04.617 --> 00:08:06.285
doesn't mean
they found nothing.

00:08:06.285 --> 00:08:08.120
Even O.J.
doesn't walk around saying,

00:08:08.120 --> 00:08:10.322
"They found none of my gloves
at the crime scene."

00:08:10.322 --> 00:08:12.958
So, clearly Trump's approach
is not working.

00:08:12.958 --> 00:08:14.193
Of course, it might not matter

00:08:14.193 --> 00:08:16.829
since we have an absurd
electoral system

00:08:16.829 --> 00:08:19.164
that lets, like,
five states choose the winner.

00:08:19.164 --> 00:08:20.833
And the winner
is often the loser.

00:08:20.833 --> 00:08:22.934
It's like when you had the
winning numbers on a scratch-off

00:08:22.934 --> 00:08:24.603
and when you looked at it,
the prize just said,

00:08:24.603 --> 00:08:27.106
"Give 10,000 bucks to the guy
standing next to you."

00:08:27.106 --> 00:08:29.508
Knowing they have an electoral
college advantage,

00:08:29.508 --> 00:08:31.610
Trump and his allies
have made no attempt

00:08:31.610 --> 00:08:33.245
to reach out
to the majority of voters

00:08:33.245 --> 00:08:35.714
that have consistently
disapproved of him

00:08:35.714 --> 00:08:37.182
since day one of his campaign.

00:08:37.182 --> 00:08:40.185
Instead, they've invested
in a two-pronged approach

00:08:40.185 --> 00:08:41.587
of distorting reality

00:08:41.587 --> 00:08:44.423
by pretending that so-called
liberal cities are in chaos.

00:08:44.423 --> 00:08:46.392
And also that the pandemic
is over

00:08:46.392 --> 00:08:48.293
and the economy is great,
none of which is true.

00:08:48.293 --> 00:08:50.529
Trump just did it
again yesterday

00:08:50.529 --> 00:08:51.731
at his press conference.

00:08:51.731 --> 00:08:54.633
-Under my leadership,
next year will be

00:08:54.633 --> 00:08:56.735
the greatest economic year
in the history of our country,

00:08:56.735 --> 00:08:57.936
I project.

00:08:57.936 --> 00:08:59.104
We're currently witnessing

00:08:59.104 --> 00:09:01.073
the fastest
labor market recovery

00:09:01.073 --> 00:09:07.346
from an economic crisis
in history, world history.

00:09:07.346 --> 00:09:10.982
By contrast, Biden presided
over the worst, the weakest,

00:09:10.982 --> 00:09:13.286
and the slowest
economic recovery

00:09:13.286 --> 00:09:14.953
since the Great Depression.

00:09:14.953 --> 00:09:17.456
It was a long, slow slog.

00:09:17.456 --> 00:09:21.193
-Listening to you read off
a script is a long, slow slog.

00:09:21.193 --> 00:09:23.795
It's like listening to Rocky
read an eye chart

00:09:23.795 --> 00:09:25.897
after ten rounds
with Apollo Creed.

00:09:25.897 --> 00:09:28.200
"A, A, A."

00:09:28.200 --> 00:09:29.869
"They're not all As, Rock!"

00:09:29.869 --> 00:09:33.138
And I'm sorry, you're calling
the Obama recovery

00:09:33.138 --> 00:09:34.639
the worst,
the weakest, and the slowest?

00:09:34.639 --> 00:09:37.343
If anything, that sounds like
an action movie franchise

00:09:37.343 --> 00:09:38.911
about your three adult children.

00:09:38.911 --> 00:09:40.713
Best thing about that joke,
you can switch them around,

00:09:40.713 --> 00:09:41.980
still works.

00:09:41.980 --> 00:09:43.749
Trump and the GOP have decided
their only choice

00:09:43.749 --> 00:09:45.850
is to spin a fantasy
alternate reality

00:09:45.850 --> 00:09:47.052
where everything is great

00:09:47.052 --> 00:09:49.021
despite the fact
that coronavirus cases

00:09:49.021 --> 00:09:51.657
are once again
on the rise in 22 states,

00:09:51.657 --> 00:09:54.160
and we've only recovered
about half the jobs

00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:56.262
that were lost in what's been
the greatest economic crash

00:09:56.262 --> 00:09:57.396
since the Great Depression.

00:09:57.396 --> 00:09:59.665
Just because some of
those jobs came back

00:09:59.665 --> 00:10:01.400
doesn't make you
an economic genius.

00:10:01.400 --> 00:10:03.669
If you gained 30 pounds
during quarantine,

00:10:03.669 --> 00:10:05.337
you can't sell
a workout tape called

00:10:05.337 --> 00:10:07.873
"How to Lose Five Pounds
&amp; That's It!"

00:10:07.873 --> 00:10:09.341
But probably Trump's most brazen

00:10:09.341 --> 00:10:11.543
and infuriating act
of reality distortion yesterday

00:10:11.543 --> 00:10:13.346
came when he tried
to con people into thinking

00:10:13.346 --> 00:10:14.880
he's an anti-war president.

00:10:14.880 --> 00:10:17.383
Trump was reacting to
the furor of "The Atlantic's"

00:10:17.383 --> 00:10:19.184
bombshell report
that he called Americans

00:10:19.184 --> 00:10:21.253
who died in war
"losers" and "suckers,"

00:10:21.253 --> 00:10:23.655
which has been confirmed
by multiple outlets

00:10:23.655 --> 00:10:25.557
including the A.P., CNN,
and even Fox News

00:10:25.557 --> 00:10:27.259
and also by common sense.

00:10:27.259 --> 00:10:29.962
I mean, it sounds exactly
like something Trump would say.

00:10:29.962 --> 00:10:33.232
He probably thinks anyone
who dies is a sucker.

00:10:33.232 --> 00:10:36.201
"I'm going to live until I'm at
least 200, just like Rudy.

00:10:36.201 --> 00:10:37.636
What's your secret, Rudy?"

00:10:37.636 --> 00:10:39.905
"You got to sweat out
the toxins, boss!"

00:10:39.905 --> 00:10:41.240
At his press conference
yesterday,

00:10:41.240 --> 00:10:43.943
Trump tried to claim
he's beloved by the troops,

00:10:43.943 --> 00:10:45.344
which is not true.

00:10:45.344 --> 00:10:48.280
Polls show active duty troops
actually prefer Joe Biden.

00:10:48.280 --> 00:10:49.915
And then he took the lie
even further, claiming

00:10:49.915 --> 00:10:51.884
Pentagon officials
don't like him

00:10:51.884 --> 00:10:54.520
because he is
against endless wars.

00:10:54.520 --> 00:10:56.255
-I'm not saying the military's
in love with me,

00:10:56.255 --> 00:10:57.889
the soldiers are.

00:10:57.889 --> 00:11:00.292
The top people in the Pentagon
probably aren't

00:11:00.292 --> 00:11:03.061
because they want to do nothing
but fight wars

00:11:03.061 --> 00:11:05.731
so that all of those
wonderful companies

00:11:05.731 --> 00:11:07.600
that make the bombs
and make the planes

00:11:07.600 --> 00:11:09.635
and make everything else
stay happy.

00:11:09.635 --> 00:11:10.936
-Oh, yeah, man, totally.

00:11:10.936 --> 00:11:12.404
Everyone believes
you're an anti-war activist.

00:11:12.404 --> 00:11:14.873
I can totally see you marching
on Washington in the '60s

00:11:14.873 --> 00:11:16.875
with a beard
and teashade glasses

00:11:16.875 --> 00:11:18.610
holding a sign
and smoking a joint.

00:11:18.610 --> 00:11:20.612
"It's like Lennon says,
give peas a chance.

00:11:20.612 --> 00:11:22.048
I mean, I've already
given peas a chance.

00:11:22.048 --> 00:11:24.216
Hard pass for me.
Not a fan of the pea."

00:11:24.216 --> 00:11:26.752
Second, this is an especially
infuriating lie,

00:11:26.752 --> 00:11:29.821
coming from a guy who has
repeatedly touted billions

00:11:29.821 --> 00:11:32.558
in arms sales to
a brutal regime in Saudi Arabia,

00:11:32.558 --> 00:11:34.526
vetoed a bill
to end U.S. involvement

00:11:34.526 --> 00:11:36.161
in the horrific war in Yemen,

00:11:36.161 --> 00:11:38.831
massively expanded bombing
campaigns across the world

00:11:38.831 --> 00:11:40.765
including a record number
in Afghanistan,

00:11:40.765 --> 00:11:43.936
increased the Pentagon's budget
for the fifth consecutive year

00:11:43.936 --> 00:11:47.239
to the point where it's now
near now Iraq War levels,

00:11:47.239 --> 00:11:49.107
added billions
to a Pentagon slush fund

00:11:49.107 --> 00:11:50.810
specifically for war fighting,

00:11:50.810 --> 00:11:53.712
and has bragged about sending
U.S. troops to Saudi Arabia

00:11:53.712 --> 00:11:56.148
because Saudi Arabia
would pay for it.

00:11:56.148 --> 00:11:58.250
Or how about the time
Trump gleefully showed off

00:11:58.250 --> 00:12:00.819
all the weapons he was selling
to Saudi Arabia's

00:12:00.819 --> 00:12:02.988
Crown Prince
Mohammad bin Salman?

00:12:02.988 --> 00:12:08.327
-If you look in terms
of dollars, $3 billion,

00:12:08.327 --> 00:12:14.767
$533 million, $525 million.

00:12:14.767 --> 00:12:16.135
That's peanuts for you.

00:12:16.135 --> 00:12:17.636
Should've increased it.

00:12:17.636 --> 00:12:23.175
$880 million.
$645 million.

00:12:23.175 --> 00:12:24.543
$6 billion.

00:12:24.543 --> 00:12:27.412
That's for frigates.

00:12:27.412 --> 00:12:28.981
$889 million.

00:12:28.981 --> 00:12:30.683
$63 million.

00:12:30.683 --> 00:12:33.385
And that's
for various artillery.

00:12:33.385 --> 00:12:36.755
THAAD system, $13 billion.

00:12:36.755 --> 00:12:38.357
[ Cameras clicking ]

00:12:38.357 --> 00:12:41.593
The C-130 heli--
airplanes,

00:12:41.593 --> 00:12:44.263
the Hercules, great plane,

00:12:44.263 --> 00:12:46.732
$3.8 billion.

00:12:46.732 --> 00:12:49.568
The Bradley vehicles,
that's the tanks,

00:12:49.568 --> 00:12:51.302
$1.2 billion.

00:12:51.302 --> 00:12:55.007
And the P-8 Poseidons,

00:12:55.007 --> 00:12:57.943
$1.4 billion.

00:12:57.943 --> 00:12:59.711
-You should've just worn
a waiter's uniform

00:12:59.711 --> 00:13:01.780
and brought the weapons in
on a dessert tray.

00:13:01.780 --> 00:13:04.450
"Would you like the Bradley
tanks or the Hercules rockets

00:13:04.450 --> 00:13:05.751
or perhaps
the chocolate mousse?"

00:13:05.751 --> 00:13:06.985
"You know what?
Should we be naughty?

00:13:06.985 --> 00:13:08.220
Should we get two?

00:13:08.220 --> 00:13:09.688
We're going to do the tanks
and the mousse

00:13:09.688 --> 00:13:11.990
and then just bring --
bring a bunch of spoons."

00:13:11.990 --> 00:13:15.327
But the story about Trump
denigrating Americans who died

00:13:15.327 --> 00:13:17.596
or were wounded in war
is such a perfect window

00:13:17.596 --> 00:13:19.831
into the reality distortion
machine on the right.

00:13:19.831 --> 00:13:22.801
Because even Fox News, whose own
national security reporter,

00:13:22.801 --> 00:13:25.036
Jennifer Griffin,
confirmed the story,

00:13:25.036 --> 00:13:26.371
has sought to undercut it.

00:13:26.371 --> 00:13:28.841
Here's how Fox treated
the story after Griffin

00:13:28.841 --> 00:13:31.042
confirmed it
with her own reporting.

00:13:31.042 --> 00:13:33.044
-Don't you find it the least
bit questionable

00:13:33.044 --> 00:13:34.747
that the Biden campaign,

00:13:34.747 --> 00:13:37.282
perhaps the slowest,
clumsiest entity

00:13:37.282 --> 00:13:41.020
since Joe Biden himself
already had an ad made

00:13:41.020 --> 00:13:43.722
based on this -- this hoax?

00:13:43.722 --> 00:13:45.057
-We also know that the story
is based

00:13:45.057 --> 00:13:46.992
on completely
anonymous sources

00:13:46.992 --> 00:13:48.793
and that anonymous sources
are participating

00:13:48.793 --> 00:13:51.997
in some kind of information
operation against the president.

00:13:51.997 --> 00:13:54.766
-You wrote there are no words
for how disgusting

00:13:54.766 --> 00:13:56.835
and dishonorable this is.

00:13:56.835 --> 00:13:59.037
My question to you is, how
do you know it's accurate?

00:13:59.037 --> 00:14:00.238
How do you know it's true?

00:14:00.238 --> 00:14:01.640
-Your own network confirmed it.

00:14:01.640 --> 00:14:03.008
Do you guys watch
your own channel,

00:14:03.008 --> 00:14:05.510
or do you just take naps
until Trump tweets something?

00:14:05.510 --> 00:14:07.613
"What? He said he didn't have
a series of mini strokes?

00:14:07.613 --> 00:14:09.214
All right, are mini strokes
even a thing?

00:14:09.214 --> 00:14:10.348
You know what,
it doesn't matter.

00:14:10.348 --> 00:14:11.816
Quick, get it on the air
and use this chyron.

00:14:11.816 --> 00:14:13.819
'A Stroke of Genius.'"

00:14:13.819 --> 00:14:15.554
And there's no better
indication of the fact

00:14:15.554 --> 00:14:17.389
that Fox is a propaganda machine

00:14:17.389 --> 00:14:19.524
and not a real news organization
than the fact

00:14:19.524 --> 00:14:22.227
that they're willing
to undercut their own reporting

00:14:22.227 --> 00:14:23.828
to serve
the president's agenda.

00:14:23.828 --> 00:14:26.231
No legitimate news organization
would do that.

00:14:26.231 --> 00:14:28.066
When the "New York Times"
reports something negative

00:14:28.066 --> 00:14:30.302
about Joe Biden,
they don't use the headline

00:14:30.302 --> 00:14:33.605
"Failing 'New York Times'
spreads fake news -- sad."

00:14:33.605 --> 00:14:35.273
Just goes to show you
they can't actually

00:14:35.273 --> 00:14:36.775
campaign on their record.

00:14:36.775 --> 00:14:38.676
So instead they're trying to
concoct an alternate universe

00:14:38.676 --> 00:14:41.112
where coronavirus is over,
the economy is back,

00:14:41.112 --> 00:14:44.083
and a president who brags
about arms sales is anti-war.

00:14:44.083 --> 00:14:45.517
If that doesn't work,
Trump will probably

00:14:45.517 --> 00:14:47.987
just try to convince people
that he's Joe Biden.

00:14:47.987 --> 00:14:49.554
"You know, I was just saying
to my wife, Jill,

00:14:49.554 --> 00:14:51.023
no more malarkey.

00:14:51.023 --> 00:14:52.491
We hate malarkey,
don't we, folks?

00:14:52.491 --> 00:14:54.726
We've had it up to here
with the malarkey."

00:14:54.726 --> 00:14:56.828
I think it's safe to say that
at this point

00:14:56.828 --> 00:14:59.331
instead of hiring the best
and the brightest,

00:14:59.331 --> 00:15:01.967
the GOP or the Trump campaign
are filled with --

00:15:01.967 --> 00:15:04.469
-The worst, the weakest,
and the slowest.

00:15:04.469 --> 00:15:06.071
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:15:06.071 --> 00:15:08.874
♪♪

